Digitalghost wrote:

> Hey all,
> 
> Nethack & Slashem SDL mode both crashed my OS/X machine. I found out
> it's because "main" is a compiler macro in SDL and SDL uses this trick
> to force initialization code into the program before any code in main
> can be executed.  The bug is that, unixmain.c does not #include "SDL/
> SDL.h" before int main, causing the compiler macro to not be invoked
> and thus causing SDL to not initialize properly.  This bug does not
> affect linux since linux apparently does not need the SDLmain
> initialization.
> 
> To fix this, put these lines at the top of unixmain.c:
> 
> #ifdef SDL_GRAPHICS
> #include "SDL/SDL.h"
> #endif


